Package: @alchemy.run/domain
Applies-to: vendor/alchemy/alchemy.run-domain-734c27a.tgz
Upstream: not yet reported
Why: The prover reads a case told with `effect/Match` and nothing a schema gives for the same question: a tagged
  union's `guards`, `isAnyOf`, `match` and `matchOrElse`, `Schema.is`, `constTrue` and `constFalse` each end a proof
  with "outside the code the prover reads", and `X.make(...)` of an event or a rejection is not the instance `new X(...)`
  builds. So the model told every case twice, once in its schema and once by hand, and built with `new` where the rest
  of the repository builds with `make`. With this the prover reads them as the library writes them, and where it cannot
  say exactly what a schema answers (a check it does not read or does not apply, a tag that is not text) it says
  "not read" and proves nothing.
Remove-when: The library's prover reads these itself. `bun run beep patches prove` then says this patch's test passes
  without it.
Test: test/alchemy-domain/03-a-schemas-own-guards/SchemaGuards.test.ts

